  "note": "Conjunction Data Message. The example is shipped as a readable .kvn file under corpus and carried here as a decode vector, hex-encoded because that is the only input form the schema has. It is the clause 3.6.2 example, which carries only the obligatory keywords. One transcription change: the Blue Book renders its minus signs as U+2212 and this uses ASCII hyphen-minus, because clause 6.3.1 allows only printable ASCII and the typography in the PDF is a rendering artefact. What the vector asserts is the conjunction \u2014 the time of closest approach, the miss distance \u2014 and for each object its identity, whether it can manoeuvre, and how many rows of covariance it carried. The numbers are floats, which a vector field cannot hold, and are checked in pkg/cdm against the same text.",
